hv/crates/vmlab-hv-devices/src/virtio/gpu/renderer.rs adapts command dispatch,
resource operations and fence-ring tracking from crosvm's
devices/src/virtio/gpu/mod.rs and virtio_gpu.rs at revision
ad804a6ecf1d3c4337f18b56092fc54d8ca574fa, Copyright 2018 The ChromiumOS
Authors. BSD-3-Clause; the complete licence is in hv/LICENSE.crosvm.

hv/crates/vmlab-hv-devices/src/usb/host/ lifts the host USB passthrough
backend from crosvm at the same revision: usb_sys/src (as sys.rs and the
ioctl-number formulas), usb_util/src/types.rs, usb_util/src/descriptor.rs
and usb_util/src/device.rs (Device/Transfer, without the mmap DMA buffer
and with URB identity as a tag instead of an Arc pointer), plus the host
backend's interface claiming, descriptor filtering and control-transfer
interception from devices/src/usb/backend/{device,host_backend} (FIDO
pruned, event-loop/job-queue plumbing replaced by the controller's poll
loop). Copyright 2018-2024 The ChromiumOS Authors. BSD-3-Clause; the
complete licence is in hv/LICENSE.crosvm. vmlab-hv's additions there —
USBDEVFS_CONNECT on detach and claim failure so host drivers rebind, the
UsbFs seam and its fake — are original.

rutabaga_gfx 0.1.80 and magma-gpu 0.1.80 are dependencies, not copied code.

- `hv/crates/vmlab-hv-devices/src/virtio/fs/fuse/` — the FUSE server stack
